# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Next.js loads .env.local itself; never commit the copy.

# The local Postgres from compose.yaml (`make db-up`). A Neon URL has the same form, with
# ?sslmode=require at the end; `neon env pull --file .env.neon` writes the Neon dev branch's
# variables to .env.neon (gitignored), kept apart so the local database stays the default.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://hackr:hackr@localhost:5433/hackr

# Migrations use the direct (unpooled) URL when it is set, as Neon provides; locally the one above
# serves both.
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=

# The import route (/api/cron/import) refuses every request unless this is set, 16 characters or
# more, and sent as "Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>". Vercel Cron sends it in production.
# Make one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=

# OpenAgenda's read key (developers.openagenda.com, "Authentification"): the daily import sends it
# in a "key" header. Without it the import reports OpenAgenda as failed and reads the other sources.
# OPENAGENDA_API_KEY=

# Language models for "Build my brief" (decision D13): a model reads a listed event's pages and gives
# each fact with the sentence it rests on; code keeps only facts whose sentences are on the page.
# OpenRouter goes first, and every request goes only to endpoints that keep no data and do not train on
# it. The model defaults to anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5, which is paid, so the key needs credits (cap it
# with a monthly limit on the key); name another model here.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=
# Requesty is the fallback, used only when both are set. The model is a free model ID or a fallback
# policy made in Requesty's dashboard ("policy/<name>"), chaining free models that support JSON schema
# and whose providers do not train on data.
# REQUESTY_API_KEY=
# REQUESTY_MODEL=
